[#:seon.task{:name "hot-internals-pay-armed-validation"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "Armed validation cost per call was Malli's regex driver for the :cat input plus -instrument-f's argument vector and always-on guard pair (~700-1300 B, 200-500 ns per armed call; ~6,600 armed calls per trivial agent form). Fixed in malli 43c6dca8 (pin c0c39ec5c), adopted at the next restart. Done when root re-runs tmp/contract-cost-opus/probe.clj on the new pin and the armed-validation share of a trivial eval (JFR, tmp/contract-cost-opus/agg.py) is measured; the remaining armed overhead is `seon.instrument/arm-var!`'s timing wrapper (~100 ns, 0 B) and the validators' own leaf work."
             :must-read #{seon.instrument/arm-var! seon.schema/canonical-reference-graph}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/perf-profile-2026-09-26.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/landing/contract-cost-opus-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-oversized-refusal-hides-its-cause"
             :kind :function
             :intent "When an armed refusal's data exceeds the admission bound (a 7,872-byte :over-bound remainder), the wrapper answers only 'X :malli.core/invalid-input: the refusal could not be built.' (instrument.clj:633), with no path, expected schema or offending shape. That is how call-reach's set-for-sequential defect showed at HEAD. The refusal must name the member and path and let the floor bound the offending value."
             :must-read #{seon.instrument/compiled-wrapper}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/task-log-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "instrumentation-is-jvm-global"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "Instrumentation and Malli's function-schema registration are process-global (2,098 installed wrappers; `seon.instrument/apply!` and malli.instrument change them for every test member), so the test runner must keep the ambient snapshot, drift and restore family and a member can damage shared Vars. Make wrappers and registrations per context so the C2 family (ambient-snapshot, restore-live-cluster-schema!, schema-restore-drift, run-vars!'s drift branch) can go in one cut."
             :must-read #{seon.instrument/apply! seon.test.runner/ambient-snapshot}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/delete-r8-r6-r10-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "contract-refusal-carries-wrapper-bookkeeping"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An agent's contract refusal reaches it with the wrapper's bookkeeping beside operation/expected/offending/problems: :seon.instrument/arglists, arity, arm, caller (\"sci.lang.Var (lang.cljc:217)\", the interpreter, never the author), check, fn (= operation), malli, problem-count, `:seon.error/expected-shape` and data-blob digests, :seon.error/doc, shown and result-id (~2.5 KB for one refused argument). Keep operation, expected, offending, problems (fix) and member; the rest is derivable from the operation's entity or is evaluation evidence. The kernel side (err-minimal-opus) already drops the evaluator's frames and the duplicated link message."
             :must-read #{seon.instrument/compiled-wrapper seon.sci.kernel/failure-value}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/err-minimal-opus-2026-09-26.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-redefines-arming-jvm-wide"
             :kind :namespace
             :intent "`seon.dev.source-instrumentation-test/source-publication-restores-contracts-after-early-reload-failure` runs with-redefs-fn over #'clojure.core/require, #'seon.instrument/apply!, #'seon.instrument/remove!, #'seon.cluster/refresh-source! and #'seon.config/effective for the whole JVM: while it runs, every concurrent member's require and every adoption's arming call the stub, and boot's armed wrapper for apply! is replaced. Found 2026-09-27 closing the whole-JVM apply! class (task e702974a368a, closed). Done when the test injects its lifecycle steps as explicit values to the owner it proves (or runs isolated), and no test rebinds these roots."
             :must-read #{seon.instrument/apply! seon.test.runner/ambient-snapshot}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/instrument-scope-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "violation-construction-is-quadratic-in-explain-errors"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.instrument/violation` (instrument.clj ~305-316) scans described-unions with some and all errors again with remove for every explain error, so building one refusal is quadratic in the error count: an armed call of seon.cluster/published-analyzer-digest with 5,445 malformed entities pinned a core for over 10 minutes (fix-boot-full-pass probe, 2026-09-27). A large invalid argument must refuse in time proportional to its errors (index described unions once; bound the errors examined, as the floor bounds what prints)."
             :must-read #{seon.instrument/violation}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/landing/boot-ready-regression-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-map-for-a-sequential-crashes-the-refusal-builder"
             :kind :function
             :intent "An armed call whose [:sequential :map] argument receives a map throws ClassCastException (clojure.lang.Keyword cannot be cast to java.util.Map$Entry) inside the refusal builder, so the caller gets only 'X :malli.core/invalid-input: the refusal could not be built' (instrument.clj:789 fallback) with no path, expected or offending member. Reproduced at default 441988b49 through seon.render.transcript/ledger-effects, which the debug-view cut deleted: any armed function with an [:sequential :map] argument given a refused read's error map reproduces it. Done when that call refuses with the member, path [2], expected [:sequential :map] and the map as offending, and a regression covers a map-for-sequential argument."
             :must-read #{seon.instrument/compiled-wrapper}
             :evidence #{"test/seon/render/web_debug_test.clj"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-re-evaluation-test-leaves-a-replaced-root"
             :kind :function
             :intent "`seon.instrument-test/re-evaluating-a-defn-silently-strips-instrumentation` evals (defn doubled ...) into seon.instrument-test with the JVM compiler and never restores the file's root, so `seon.instrument-test/doubled` keeps a NO_SOURCE_PATH class for the JVM's life: `seon.instrument-test/a-root-replaced-outside-a-reload-is-named` is red in every later run (serial included), and runtime_status reports replaced-roots 1. Done when the re-evaluation probe uses its own interned Var (or an SCI context) and both tests pass in either order in one JVM."
             :must-read #{seon.instrument/replaced-roots}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/test-agents-concurrency-2026-09-27.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-contract-with-an-fn-ifn-cannot-arm-on-a-sci-branch"
             :kind :function
             :intent "A contract containing [:fn clojure.core/ifn?] cannot arm on a SCI branch (\"No reader function for tag object\"): how the spec is stored and read back (my-program-reads lane, 67b4d420b). Done when a stored spec with a registered named predicate arms on a branch and the failing form is a regression."
             :must-read #{seon.schema/register!}}]
